{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523540-some-questions-about-playing-as-a-ghoul","id":1523540,"title":"Some questions about playing as a ghoul","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-04T04:58:43-07:00","id":1523540,"title":"Some questions about playing as a ghoul","content":"We are playing the Dark Ages and I want to create a ghoul character that has, potentially, lost his domitor and therefore became an independent ghoul. The other player is willing to play an independent ghoul as well and our gm agrees on that, so there are some questions about the mechanics and lore:<br /> <br /> 1. How long a ghoul can live?<br /> 2. Can ghouls of a 7th Generation domitor learn Disciplines other than Potence and up to wich level?<br /> 3. Are there any negative or positive outcomes of consuming the blood of different vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28215-madislak","name":"Madislak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T05:51:59-07:00","id":1523544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madislak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523540-some-questions-about-playing-as-a-ghoul#post1523540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. How long a ghoul can live?</div> </div> </div> </div>As long as a ghoul has vitae in their system, they don't age and theoretically can exist as long as a vampire as long as they have a consistent vitae supply. The trick is that they automatically burn one blood point every month to maintain ghoul status. If they use up all their stored BPs or just go without for long enough, then their ghoul status ends, at which point they physically age to their true age. So a 20 something ghoul who has been around for over a century will age to death as soon as they run out of vitae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madislak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523540-some-questions-about-playing-as-a-ghoul#post1523540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Can ghouls of a 7th Generation domitor learn Disciplines other than Potence and up to wich level?</div> </div> </div> </div>A ghoul can learn any Discipline the domitor knows, usually with a great amount of effort. The three physical disciplines of Potence, Fortitude and Celerity are considered instinctive and thus can always be learned by a ghoul, hence why animal ghouls have access to them. Though if they lose ghoul status, then they can't access the disciplines in any form until the consume more vitae.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madislak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523540-some-questions-about-playing-as-a-ghoul#post1523540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Are there any negative or positive outcomes of consuming the blood of different vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>By RAW, consuming Nosferatu blood can have a mutagenic affect on the ghoul. Usually this just makes the human somewhat ugly in some fashion, but in animals it causes considerable size increases, think of cockroaches the size of footballs or rats the size of a dog, needless to say an alligator ghoul gets to the size of the critter from the Lake Placid movie. A human ghoul takes on personality quirks of that clan. A ghoul dosed on Brujah blood will be more prone to frenzy and acting up, a malkavian ghoul will have all sorts of mental issues, a ventrue ghoul will become obsessed with only consuming ventrue vitae, Setite ghouls become photosensitive, etc.<br /> <br /> The main issue is blood bonding, after three feedings they are hooked and submissive. So an independent ghoul has to constantly get different donors, until the previous donor is out of their system. On the flip side a fully blood bonded ghoul can guzzle another vampires vitae without worrying about forming a new blood bond. Though it is possible to overdose on vitae at which point you start having all sorts of problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-04T09:46:22-07:00","id":1523558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madislak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523540-some-questions-about-playing-as-a-ghoul#post1523540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are playing the Dark Ages and I want to create a ghoul character that has, potentially, lost his domitor and therefore became an independent ghoul. The other player is willing to play an independent ghoul as well and our gm agrees on that, so there are some questions about the mechanics and lore:<br /> <br /> 1. How long a ghoul can live?<br /> <br /> As long as they have vampire blood on a regular basis, there aging process halts and any long term illness will not out progress further. If they outlive a natural span of life and don't get vitae anymore then they will age rapidly and die. The Revenant Ghoul families have a slowed aging process and maturation process then most but that is another topic alltogether. <br /> <br /> <br /> 2. Can ghouls of a 7th Generation domitor learn Disciplines other than Potence and up to wich level?<br /> <br /> As far as I know and I have to look up Ghouls Fatal Addiction again, but Ghouls can learn other Disciplines if their Dominator is willing to invest the time and depending on the generation and age of the Kindred, you could have some that could match a typical Elder, but they are quite rare and are usually belong to the Methsulath category and they are regarded with a certain level of fear in Kindred &amp; Ghoul society<br /> <br /> 3. Are there any negative or positive outcomes of consuming the blood of different vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most times they take on traits of the clan that they serve.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T05:08:30-07:00","id":1523620,"title":"","content":"Random ghoul related question of my own, to learn a non-clan discipline a vampire requires a teacher which usually means a Boon owed or cashed in and the potential for blood bond shenanigans.<br /> <br /> But if any ghoul can instinctively learn Celerity, Fortitude, and Potence; does that mean they can teach those disciplines to their Domitor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-05T13:59:06-07:00","id":1523659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1523540-some-questions-about-playing-as-a-ghoul?p=1523620#post1523620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Random ghoul related question of my own, to learn a non-clan discipline a vampire requires a teacher which usually means a Boon owed or cashed in and the potential for blood bond shenanigans.<br /> <br /> But if any ghoul can instinctively learn Celerity, Fortitude, and Potence; does that mean they can teach those disciplines to their Domitor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they could and sometimes Ghouls are used to teach their master many other skills if needed. I believe I heard in Archons &amp; Templars that there was one Sabbat member who had a ghoul whom he or she kept around to learn as much about forensic science they could before getting rid of said ghoul. Another thing to take in account is how powerful the ghoul Dominator is as ones who served a 4th-6th generation monster cam be quite well versed in the Disciplines as oppossed to my 11th generation Malkavian who wouldn't be able to make powerful ghouls by how much weaker he is in comparasion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 10-05-2023, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T02:43:43-07:00","id":1523690,"title":"","content":"One more question here. I came up with an idea of a former thrall of Baltic origin, that was taken captive by Scandinavians. After the storm he with his owner were the only survivors on their broken drakkar, and because of a moment of hesitation, he was able to severely damage his owner and escape. Surviving on Swedish shores, he got the attention of a Tzimisce, who saw some potential in his will to survive. And so, to study him further, Tzimisce made him their ghoul. So to study how this ghoul will survive in a hostile area, using only their body to hunt for food and defend himself against the animals and humans, this Tzimisce either taught him to use Vicissitude, or altered him themselves grafting him, say, wings. Is it possible lore-wise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28215,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28215-madislak","user":"Madislak","date":". 04-20-2024, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28215-madislak","name":"Madislak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T10:05:53-07:00","id":1523721,"title":"","content":"A Tzimisce grafting someone to themselves has been mentioned in the lore with Veyla &amp; Gesu being the examples. I don't think that there is a mechanical rule in place for a player character to my limited knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T10:52:00-07:00","id":1523725,"title":"","content":"<i>Ghouls - Fatal Addiction</i> has the variable cost Vicissitude Modifications Merit. Wings are a 4pt modification, you can glide but not fly under your own power. Claws are 2pt, armor 3pt, fangs 1pt. If you don't know the Discipline, the alterations are permanent and can not be healed.<br /> <br /> If I recall correctly there is a similar system for Gargoyles to purchase various body traits, that could also be plundered. But in general, playing a ghouled Vicissitude monstrosity is possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-06T13:37:02-07:00","id":1523734,"title":"","content":"Thank you everyone! Seems like playing as a ghoul will be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28215-madislak","name":"Madislak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T12:03:57-07:00","id":1523778,"title":"","content":"I didn't remember that bit in Ghoul Fatal Addiction Voidshaper, but I should've as I try to take some care in creating Ghoul NPC'S for my Kindred player characters and what kind of servant I want them to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T12:07:54-07:00","id":1523779,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28215-madislak\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28215\" data-vbnamecard=\"28215\">Madislak</a> it should be possible for your Ghoul to learn Visscuitiude or at least the basics depending on what generation the Fiend is in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}